{"type":"text","timestamp":1785134432209,"sessionID":"ses_05db25534ffez000JPR32B4DBM","part":{"id":"prt_fa24db5db001ShVMkPqLCWbnO2","messageID":"msg_fa24dad47001qNS69oJNIBRD5c","sessionID":"ses_05db25534ffez000JPR32B4DBM","type":"text","text":"**PainPal – Day 4‑5 Architecture (≈185 words)**  \n\nThe platform is built on a modern, cloud‑native stack that separates concerns while keeping latency low for interactive therapy.  \n\n**Front‑end** – A React 18 single‑page app written in TypeScript uses MUI for accessible, responsive UI components. Static assets are deployed to Vercel’s edge CDN, enabling fast global delivery and automatic preview builds. Authentication tokens are stored in HttpOnly cookies, and the client integrates Twilio Programmable Video SDK for secure, HIPAA‑compatible live sessions.  \n\n**Back‑end / API** – An Express server (Node + TypeScript) runs in Docker containers orchestrated by AWS Fargate, providing auto‑scaling compute. The API layer is split into three micro‑services:  \n\n1. **Auth & Subscription Service** – Handles JWT login, role‑based access, Stripe webhook processing, and synchronises subscription status with a PostgreSQL RDS store.  \n2. **Exercise Library & Planner** – Exposes CRUD endpoints for a curated set of physiotherapy videos and runs a rule‑based engine that matches user‑reported pain zones to personalized exercise plans.  \n3. **Live Therapy Hub** – Manages calendar scheduling, therapist‑user matchmaking, and Twilio video room provisioning; session recordings are optionally stored in S3 for later review.  \n\n**Data Layer** – Core relational data (users, subscriptions, exercise metadata) resides in PostgreSQL; Redis Elasticache supplies fast session caching and rate‑limiting.  \n\n**Community** – Primary forum integration uses Discourse via SSO; a lightweight fallback forum (Node + SQLite) is ready if Discourse deployment stalls.  \n\n**Top Risks & Mitigations** –  \n- *Regulatory compliance*: encrypt all PHI at rest/in transit, store minimal health data, and run regular HIPAA/GDPR audits.  \n- *Therapist availability*: maintain a pool of on‑demand freelance PTs and provide pre‑recorded guided sessions as a fallback.  \n\n**Fallback Scope** – If needed, replace Twilio with access‑controlled private YouTube streams, swap Discourse for a simple React‑PostgreSQL forum, and launch initially with self‑guided exercise plans only, postponing live therapy to a later sprint.","time":{"start":1785134429659,"end":1785134432196}}}
